WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.768
-Thank you for coming by
and coming back.

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:03.769
I have so many things
to talk to you about.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.638
There are so many projects

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.739
that you do.
-A lot of content.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.174
-You are so hot right now.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.275
I can't even tell you, man.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.376
Thanks for doing that bit,
by the way,

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.278
earlier in the show.
You're a good man.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.346
But you have "Addams Family 2."

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.581
You have "The Card Counter,"

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:16.616
which I want to get into.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.384
I want to talk about "Dune"...

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.953
[ Cheering and applause ]
-"Dune."

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.388
-..."Scenes from a Marriage."

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.023
I'm not completely finished
with it yet,

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.324
but you're so good
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.494
-in that thing
and Jessica is so great

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.694
in this thing.
Gosh,

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:29.929
you guys crushed that one.
-It's heavy stuff.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.397
-Ooh! It's heavy stuff.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.433
-But I mean, when you
do these intense scenes,

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.469
what do you do to just unwind

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.071
or just go like,
"I just need a break"

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.605
or do you sit in your trailer,
or what do you do?

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.375
-Yeah, well, we had these rooms,
like greenrooms,

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.277
because we were just filming
in this --

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.478
it's like an old warehouse.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.180
It's a studio, now,
up in The Bronx.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.281
And so we had
these two little rooms

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:51.050
or individual little setups
in there.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.853
And so sometimes Jessica and I
would sit on her couch

00:00:54.853 --> 00:00:57.857
and have tea and watch
"The Great British Bake Off."

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.892
[ Laughter ]
-Is that how you...?

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.661
"Great British Bake Off."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.895
And then, sometimes she --
-It is calming.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.965
-It's really calming and sweet,
nice people.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.233
-That's the best.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.068
I love hearing that story.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.536
And then, sometimes
with maybe potato chips

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.338
and "Succession,"
that we would watch.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.439
[ Laughter ]
-Ooh.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.207
Dude, I'm getting ready
for "Succession."

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:16.776
-Oof. I can't wait.
-Right?

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.043
-Can't wait.
-It's going to be good.

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.312
-It's going
to be good.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.747
-Can I talk about "Dune"
for a second as well?

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.816
Now, "Dune," it's massive.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.351
-How do you get involved
with this?

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.552
Are you a fan of the book?
Are you a fan

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.254
of the film?
-It's a book?

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.388
[ Laughter ]
Did they make a book

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:31.324
out of it already?
-Yeah, the book came

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.358
-Fast.
-after the movie.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.527
-They make 'em fast, nowadays.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.529
-Dude, yeah, but how do you
get involved in that?

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.697
Just they call you and they go,
"Hey, we love ya"?

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:42.368
-No, I called --
I write to Denis and I say,

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.969
"Hey, I hear you're doing
'Dune.'

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:46.071
Big fan over here."

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:48.708
And then he wrote back,
"So you're a fan of Dune.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:49.909
Interesting."

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.043
[ Laughter ]
That was it.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:52.178
Didn't hear anything
for two years.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.279
[ Laughter ]
-You're joking.
-No.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.547
-That's the worst.
-And he reached out

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.482
and said that, you know,
"Here's a script.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:59.485
I'm not sure exactly
where you fit into it.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.287
Read it.
Tell me what you think."

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.855
And so I read it.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:07.025
And I already had a sense
that like Duke Leto, the dad,

00:02:07.025 --> 00:02:08.561
that's kind of, you know.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.197
The way he's even described
in the book is olive-skinned

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.865
and, you know,
the high cheekbones.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.101
And I just knew there was
a beard waiting

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.569
[ Laughter ]
to be explored.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.371
-You have the best beard game
in the business.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.540
-He walks in beard first,
you know?

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.774
[ Laughter ]
Any room.
-Of course.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.943
-And so I was ready
to unleash that one.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.911
-But, when I first met you
and you were like this,

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.314
sans beard,
and then, I see you with a beard

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.849
and, man, I was like jealous.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.183
[ Laughter ]
-Thanks, man.

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.119
You guys, have you seen this?
-[Indistinct], right?

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.720
-No, I got a patchy.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.088
[ Laughter ]
-Mm.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.257
-Quest, can I get a drumroll,
please, for this beard?

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:41.260
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.328
♪♪

00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:44.497
There you go right there.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.633
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.901
-You got a real beautiful
beard over there.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:49.969
-Tariq's got a good beard.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.136
He's got a good beard
game going,

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:53.506
but that's what I'm talk
about, right there.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.641
"Dune" beard
is what I'm talking about.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.310
And I know, in the film,

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.545
Timothée Chalamet
is your son.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:00.713
-He's my little boy.
-That's hilarious.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.814
"My little boy."
-My sweet little baby boy.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:02.815
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:03.950
-How did you guys bond?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.485
-I just would hold him a lot.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:08.421
[ Laughter ]
-That's funny.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.157
-He was the best because,
you know, it's like,

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.758
I can't just be like,
"I'm your dad."

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.427
[ Laughter ]
-Of course not.
-So he's got to

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:17.429
treat me like that, you know?
And it's that old adage,

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:18.797
you know, from theater school
where it's like

00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:20.666
the king doesn't show
the audience who the king is.

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.434
It's the court
that tells the audience

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:23.536
who the king is, you know?
-Ah.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.071
-It's because it's
how everybody else acts.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.340
-Correct.
-And so he immediately

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.509
just like, went there with it
and, you know,

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:31.844
it just shows what a,
you know,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.979
talented and beautiful
actor he is.

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:35.481
-I was going to say,
did you play him any lullabies

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.549
that you play to your son?

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.784
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.686
-We played a lot of music.
We did. We did.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:40.953
He was playing a lot of guitar
at the time,

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:42.755
so we would, you know,
we'd trade some songs

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.057
back and forth.
-I know you're a musician,

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.426
but I mean,
you play some lullabies

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:47.927
for your son.
-I do.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.395
-Yeah.
And is your wife --

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.529
-Well, I used to.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:52.331
He doesn't like them anymore.
-He's out?

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.900
[ Laughter ]
-He's out.
He's not into it anymore.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.568
-What were the songs about?
-You know, it's like

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.902
all the old crap, you know,

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:59.671
like "The Wheels on the Bus"
and the...

00:03:59.671 --> 00:04:01.206
-Classics?
-Yeah, all the classics.

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:02.508
He just wants to hear the hits.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.842
[ Laughter ]
-So he lights a lighter.

00:04:03.842 --> 00:04:05.778
[ Laughter ]
He's like, "I'm tired.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.279
I heard this one."
-I got a lot of originals,

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:09.715
but he just, you know,
he's just not as into them.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.317
-What are the originals?

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.952
-You know,
"Elephants Are Kind to People."

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.286
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:16.989
-Oh, that's a good one, yeah.
-"The Hippopotamus Song."

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.192
Although, that one,
the little guy is really into.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.094
And I feel like he's coming
around to it now,

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:23.696
the older one.
-"The Hippopotamus"?

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.231
-Yeah.
-Yeah. I mean,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.432
and it's just you on guitar?

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.800
-Yeah.
-Oh.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.935
-And singing and --
-I'm just saying because...

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.670
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.139
-You want me
to sing you a lullaby?

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.407
-Would you?

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.575
-Alright. You guys want
to hear the hippo song?

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:38.211
[ Cheering and applause ]
Want to hear the hippo song?

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:39.511
Here, here's a pick, right here.

00:04:39.511 --> 00:04:40.680
-Alright, a pick, too.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.247
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:44.149
-Alright, [indistinct]

00:04:44.149 --> 00:04:47.653
